{"id": 8702, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">A</mark> 38-year-old woman is brought to the emergency department after a motor vehicle collision.\u00a0 She sustained no injuries in the collision but is adamant she did not see the car that hit her along the front side of her vehicle.\u00a0 The patient also reports that she has been having daily headaches and has not menstruated in the last 4 months.\u00a0 On physical examination, there is bitemporal hemianopia but no other abnormalities.\u00a0 MRI of the brain is shown below.</p><div class=\"mb-4 text-start flex justify-start items-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"w-full\"><button class=\"lg:max-w-lg md:max-w-md w-fit max-w-full my-5 hover:scale-[1.01] transition-[transform,_box-shadow] ease-in-out duration-500 hover:shadow-lg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-none\" src=\"../../Assets/images/k5smk3epp0uoo9df6nglj720.png\"/></button></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient's lesion most likely originates from which of the following embryologic layers?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "options": [{"label": "A", "text": "Endoderm"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Mesoderm"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Neural crest"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Neural tube"}, {"label": "E", "text": "Notochord"}, {"label": "F", "text": "Surface ectoderm"}], "correctAnswer": "F", "explanation": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-explanation\"><span class=\"\"><div id=\"div_T40971\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"relative max-w-full\"><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute left-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-r from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 bottom-0 w-8 z-10 transition-opacity duration-200 bg-gradient-to-l from-white dark:from-nbme-primary-dark-800 warm:from-egg-sour-50 to-transparent opacity-0\"></div><div class=\"max-w-full overflow-x-auto [&amp;_td]:min-w-[8rem] [&amp;_th]:min-w-[8rem]\"><table class=\"border bg-transparent dark:text-white border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white hover:bg-transparent warm:hover:bg-transparent dark:hover:bg-transparent cursor-default mt-2 mb-3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tbody style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-50\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">E</mark>mbryologic derivatives</strong></p></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" rowspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Ectoderm</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Surface ectoderm</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Anterior pituitary (Rathke pouch)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Lens &amp; cornea</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Inner ear sensory organs, olfactory epithelium</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Nasal &amp; oral epithelial linings, salivary glands</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Epidermis, sweat &amp; mammary glands</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Neural tube</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Brain &amp; spinal cord</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Posterior pituitary, pineal gland</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Retina</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Neural crest</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Neural ganglia, adrenal medulla</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Schwann cells; pia &amp; arachnoid mater</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Aorticopulmonary septum &amp; endocardial cushions</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Branchial arches (bones &amp; cartilage)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Skull bones</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Melanocytes</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Mesoderm</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Muscles (skeletal, cardiac &amp; smooth)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Connective tissue, bone &amp; cartilage</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Serosal linings (eg, peritoneum)</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Cardiovascular &amp; lymphatic system</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Spleen &amp; hemopoietic cells</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Kidney &amp; ureters, internal genitalia</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Adrenal cortex</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"2\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Endoderm</p></td><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><ul class=\"flex flex-col justify-start items-start list-inside list-disc ml-4 mb-4\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Gastrointestinal tract, liver, pancreas</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Lungs</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Thymus, parathyroids, thyroid follicular cells</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Middle ear epithelium</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Bladder &amp; urethra</li><li class=\"mb-1\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Parafollicular (C) cells*</li></ul></td></tr><tr class=\"hover:bg-original-nbme-400/10 warm:hover:bg-brown-700/10 dark:hover:bg-white/15\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><td class=\"border border-collapse border-black warm:border-brown-800 dark:border-white p-1\" colspan=\"3\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">*Formerly thought to be of neural crest origin.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">This patient with <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-k2h8dwqd5tlmgpb6dpui0f2j\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-k2h8dwqd5tlmgpb6dpui0f2j\">pituitary enlargement</a> on brain imaging and <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-ekoc191m470v8crolwlpupfp\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-ekoc191m470v8crolwlpupfp\">bitemporal hemianopia</a> (ie, temporal visual field loss due to compression of the optic chiasm) most likely has a <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">pituitary adenoma</strong>.\u00a0 These benign tumors arise from the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">anterior pituitary</strong> and are the most common cause of sellar masses in adults.\u00a0 Secondary hypogonadism (eg, <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">amenorrhea</strong>) frequently occurs in patients with pituitary tumors, and can be caused by excessive prolactin secretion (which suppresses hypothalamic secretion of GnRH) or direct compression of gonadotrope cells by the expanding mass.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">All tissues are derivatives of the 3 primary germ layers (ectoderm, mesoderm, endoderm) that form during <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-g0fowy875e9kbd6ub4s9xzox\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-g0fowy875e9kbd6ub4s9xzox\">gastrulation</a>.\u00a0 As epiblast cells migrate downward through the primitive streak to form the mesoderm and endoderm layers, a portion of them also migrate cranially through the primitive node (the cephalic end of the primitive streak) to form a midline, mesoderm-derived cellular cord known as the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-uwp2hep058rmi92yrpf9nr9i\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-uwp2hep058rmi92yrpf9nr9i\">notochord</a>.\u00a0 The notochord induces the overlying ectoderm to differentiate into the neuroectoderm and form the neural plate, which gives rise to the neural crest and neural tube <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices C and D)</strong>; the remainder of the ectoderm becomes the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">surface ectoderm</strong>.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">The anterior pituitary is derived from the <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Rathke pouch</strong>, an evagination of the <a class=\"hint\" data-exhibit-id=\"exhibit-xpsziqwz66mypg5q3eeqlz1l\" href=\"#exhibit-exhibit-xpsziqwz66mypg5q3eeqlz1l\">surface ectoderm</a> that lines the fetal oral cavity <strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choices A and B)</strong>.\u00a0 In contrast, the posterior pituitary (pars nervosa and pituitary stalk) is derived from the infundibulum, an extension of neuroectoderm from the diencephalon; posterior pituitary tumors are rare.</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">(Choice E)</strong>\u00a0 The notochord becomes the nucleus pulposus of the intervertebral discs in adults</p><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><strong style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">Educational objective:</strong>Pituitary adenoma is a benign tumor arising from the anterior pituitary and the most common cause of sellar masses (headache, bitemporal hemianopia, hypogonadism) in adults.\u00a0 The anterior pituitary forms from the surface ectoderm, one of the 3 tissues derived from the ectoderm (ie, surface ectoderm, neural tube, neural crest).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c</p></span></div>", "educationalObjective": "Pituitary adenoma is a benign tumor arising from the anterior pituitary and the most common cause of sellar masses (headache, bitemporal hemianopia, hypogonadism) in adults.  The anterior pituitary forms from the surface ectoderm, one of the 3 tissues derived from the ectoderm (ie, surface ectoderm, neural tube, neural crest).\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c